From: NobiTerminal fork
Date: 2026-11-20
Subject: [PATCH] a52: use avcodec_get_supported_config() for FFmpeg 9

FFmpeg 9 removed the AVCodec.sample_fmts field (deprecated since
FFmpeg 7 in favour of avcodec_get_supported_config()). The a52
plugin used rec->codec->sample_fmts[0] to pick the encoder's first
supported sample format, which no longer compiles against FFmpeg 9
headers (error: no member named 'sample_fmts' in 'struct AVCodec').

Replace it with avcodec_get_supported_config(NULL, codec,
AV_CODEC_CONFIG_SAMPLE_FORMAT, ...), which returns the same
first-supported-format list (terminated by AV_SAMPLE_FMT_NONE).
If the codec reports all formats supported (NULL list), fall back
to AV_SAMPLE_FMT_FLT, the AC3 encoder's native format.

This is the only use of a removed AVCodec field in alsa-plugins
1.2.12 (verified by source grep). Upstream has not fixed this yet
(alsa-plugins 1.2.12 is current upstream as of 2026-11-20); the
fix is fork-side until upstream adopts it.
---
 a52/pcm_a52.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/a52/pcm_a52.c b/a52/pcm_a52.c
--- a/a52/pcm_a52.c
+++ b/a52/pcm_a52.c
@@ -1202,8 +1202,16 @@
 	rec->io.flags = SND_PCM_IOPLUG_FLAG_BOUNDARY_WA;
 #endif
 #ifdef USE_AVCODEC_FRAME
-	rec->av_format = rec->codec->sample_fmts[0];
-	rec->is_planar = av_sample_fmt_is_planar(rec->av_format);
+	{
+		const enum AVSampleFormat *fmts = NULL;
+		if (avcodec_get_supported_config(NULL, rec->codec,
+						 AV_CODEC_CONFIG_SAMPLE_FORMAT, 0,
+						 (const void **)&fmts, NULL) < 0 || !fmts)
+			fmts = NULL;
+		/* NULL list means all formats supported; AC3 is natively float. */
+		rec->av_format = fmts ? fmts[0] : AV_SAMPLE_FMT_FLT;
+	}
+	rec->is_planar = av_sample_fmt_is_planar(rec->av_format);
 #else
 	rec->av_format = AV_SAMPLE_FMT_S16;
 #endif
